<p class="note">
  Whoever holds the database credentials can read the database — no schema prevents that.
  What a schema <b>can</b> do is make access deliberate, logged, and visible to the partner
  whose data it is. <code>audit_log</code> is append-only, enforced by triggers.
</p>
